+/* One parsed instruction operand.  CLS is the opcode table letter it
+   matches.  A fixed operand - A, AB, C, DPTR, @A+DPTR, @A+PC, @DPTR, @Ri,
+   Rn - is its own letter and REG its register number; '#' is an
+   immediate and '/' a complemented bit.  'D' is a byte that can only be
+   a direct address: a special function register or an ARn written by
+   name, or a HIGH()/LOW() half.  'B' is an operand that can only be a
+   bit: a bit written by name, ACC.7, 0x20.3, sym.3 or B2B().  'E' is any
+   other expression, which is a direct address, a bit or a code address
+   according to the row it is matched against.  */
